---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SubNav from '../components/SubNav.astro';
import SubFooter from '../components/SubFooter.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import rowhouseStreet from '../assets/pages/rowhouse-street.jpg';
import rowhouseDusk from '../assets/pages/rowhouse-dusk.jpg';
import chassisKit from '../assets/pages/chassis-kit.jpg';
import interiorFamily from '../assets/pages/interior-family.jpg';
import stairLight from '../assets/pages/stair-light.jpg';
import blockCorner from '../assets/pages/block-corner.jpg';
import towerDusk from '../assets/pages/tower-dusk.jpg';
import scandiAerial from '../assets/pages/scandi-aerial.jpg';
import interiorDining from '../assets/pages/interior-dining.jpg';
import gardenBeds from '../assets/pages/afternoon-garden.jpg';

const description =
  'A catalog of healthy, attainable homes: factory-precise, light-filled, efficient, and designed for the neighborhoods they sit in.';
---

<Layout title="Homes" description={description}>
  <SubNav current="/homes" />

  <section class="pt-12 md:pt-16">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm">
        <Image src={rowhouseStreet} alt="A street of warm timber rowhouses with front stoops." widths={[800, 1376]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 1100px, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" loading="eager" />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Homes</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-forest-700 md:text-5xl">Healthy, beautiful, attainable. Pick all three.</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-6">A catalog of homes designed once, built with factory precision, and repeated until the price comes down and the quality goes up. That is how every other essential product got good. Homes are next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={chassisKit} alt="An exploded view of a timber home building kit: modules, windows, stairs, and panels." widths={[700, 1376]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The kit</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Designed once. Built like a product.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">Each home is a kit of healthy parts: timber structure, high-performance windows, real insulation, quiet ventilation, engineered to go together the same way every time. Repetition is what buys the precision, and precision is what makes deep comfort and low energy bills attainable instead of luxury.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section bg-cream-50">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Inside</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Light, air, quiet, warmth.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">Natural materials that age well. Daylight in every room. Air that is filtered and fresh, walls that keep the weather out and the quiet in. Homes engineered so that comfort is the default and the utility bill is the proof.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={interiorFamily} alt="A family in a light-filled timber living room." widths={[700, 1376]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={stairLight} alt="A timber stairwell washed in daylight." widths={[700, 1376]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="md:order-2 overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={rowhouseDusk} alt="Rowhouses at dusk with warm lit windows." widths={[700, 1376]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      <div class="md:order-1">
        <p class="eyebrow">Attainable, honestly</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Smaller, smarter, and yours.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">Attainability is a design decision, not a discount. Efficient layouts that live larger than their square footage, because the neighborhood itself is part of your home: the market is your pantry, the courtyard is your second living room, the street is where your kids play. And we are building ownership paths so the people who live here can hold a piece of the place.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section bg-cream-50">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Catalog</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700 md:text-4xl">For sale and for rent. Pick your shape.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">We are designing these now, with input from the people who plan to live in them, and building custom home designer tools so you can shape your own. Nothing below is final. That is the point: tell us what you would actually want.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={rowhouseStreet} alt="Timber townhomes with stoops." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">To own</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Townhomes</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">Front doors on the street, stoops, two to three bedrooms, and a block that knows your name.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={blockCorner} alt="A mid-rise corner building with ground-floor life." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">To rent</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Apartments &amp; lofts</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">Studios to family-sized, light-filled and efficient, steps from the market and the courtyard.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={scandiAerial} alt="A courtyard block from above." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">Rent or own</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">The Scandi Block</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">Courtyard living: a quiet garden heart, daily life at the edges, and the whole block as your backyard.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={interiorDining} alt="A generous shared dining room." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">To rent</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Co-living</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">Private rooms, generous shared kitchens and long tables, priced for starting out and built for company.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={gardenBeds} alt="Garden beds between homes with several generations tending them." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">Flexible</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Multigenerational</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">Homes that flex as families grow, age, and come back together: paired flats, in-law suites, shared courtyards.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white overflow-hidden">
          <Image src={towerDusk} alt="A slender timber residential tower at dusk." widths={[600, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[3/2] h-auto w-full object-cover" />
          <figcaption class="p-5"><span class="eyebrow !text-[10px]">An open question</span><h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg text-forest-700">The urban tower</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-700">A taller idea we are testing: small footprint, big views, the district at your feet. Love it or hate it, we want to hear which.</p></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="homes-form" class="py-section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Demand first</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700 md:text-4xl">Tell us what you would want.</h2>
      <p class="prose-body mt-4">We form the community before the buildings. Reservations will lead construction the way orders lead production everywhere else, so your answer here is not a survey. It is the order book taking shape.</p>
      <form
        action="https://nowcitylabs.us19.list-manage.com/subscribe/post?u=88bfb2c8f34fdd20e85cce03f&amp;id=5812d18a23&amp;f_id=0099bbe7f0"
        method="post"
        target="_blank"
        novalidate
        class="mt-8 grid gap-5"
      >
        <div>
          <label for="EMAIL" class="block text-sm font-medium text-forest-800">Email <span class="text-copper-400">*</span></label>
          <input id="EMAIL" name="EMAIL" type="email" required autocomplete="email" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-base text-forest-800 placeholder:text-stone-400 focus:border-forest-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-forest-700/20" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="FNAME" class="block text-sm font-medium text-forest-800">First name <span class="text-copper-400">*</span></label>
          <input id="FNAME" name="FNAME" type="text" required autocomplete="given-name" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-base text-forest-800 placeholder:text-stone-400 focus:border-forest-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-forest-700/20" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="LOCATION" class="block text-sm font-medium text-forest-800">Where would you want a Now City neighborhood?</label>
          <input id="LOCATION" name="LOCATION" type="text" placeholder="city, metro, or ZIP" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-base text-forest-800 placeholder:text-stone-400 focus:border-forest-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-forest-700/20" />
        </div>
        <fieldset>
          <legend class="block text-sm font-medium text-forest-800">If a home opened up, what would catch your eye?</legend>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-stone-500">Optional. Pick anything that fits.</p>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][64]" class="accent-forest-700" /> An apartment to rent</label>
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][128]" class="accent-forest-700" /> A loft to rent</label>
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][256]" class="accent-forest-700" /> A penthouse to rent</label>
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][512]" class="accent-forest-700" /> A condo to own</label>
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][1024]" class="accent-forest-700" /> A townhome to own</label>
            <label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm text-forest-800 hover:border-forest-700/40 has-[:checked]:border-forest-700 has-[:checked]:bg-forest-700/5"><input type="checkbox" name="group[181121][2048]" class="accent-forest-700" /> Curious about all of it</label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <div style="position:absolute;left:-5000px" aria-hidden="true"><input type="text" name="b_88bfb2c8f34fdd20e85cce03f_5812d18a23" tabindex="-1" value="" /></div>
        <div class="mt-2"><button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Count me in</button></div>
      </form>
      <p class="prose-body mt-6 !text-sm text-stone-500">Drawn to the Scandi Block, co-living, multigenerational, or the tower? <a href="mailto:erik@nowcitylabs.com?subject=Homes%3A%20what%20I%27d%20want">Tell us directly</a>, one line is plenty, and it goes straight into the design conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SubFooter />
</Layout>
